[Music]  okay everybody this is my spoiler review  of the northmen make sure you see the  film first before you watch this review  i was very excited for this film i'm a  huge robert eggers fan my favorite still  being the witch and then the lighthouse  i thought was excellent too not as good  as the witch but still loved it and this  film a little worried going in because i  know it was a different genre it still  had its taste of horror in it but it's  this big epic now revenge tale and i was  curious how robert eggers was going to  approach that especially the bigger  budget not being on a 24 anymore now  he's with focus features and seeing what  was going to come out of that and now  he's got also a different co-writer  which he does every film but this one  was co-written by  shone so  my thing about this film when you watch  it and i think that it just does  everything right in the department of  making a really strong revenge epic  viking tale right and that  the brutality of it  everything is so intense in it but  what was so disappointing about it to me  was knowing who's behind it in robert  eggers and that his films with the  lighthouse and the witch  you feel something from it and  you are thinking about it for days after  right it's a really smart script those  stories and that they end on like a  haunting  visual that stays with you it sticks  with you you feel right and that's the  most important thing of the films and  that's why i was worried he was doing a  revenge tale because a lot of times  you're just kind of  watching through one character's eyes  you know where it's going there's not  much leeway to be had and i was worried  that was going to kind of be a trap for  him and i do think it was eventually a  trap for him and i think that  it does what you need to do right to  make a good revenge story right and that  i enjoyed everything that was happening  in front of me i was very entertained by  it but there's this nagging thing in  your head if you felt this way that i  felt watching it that i know who's  behind this i know he's a guy who's  known for smart stories and why is this  story not trying that why isn't it  stimulating my brain why am i not  feeling anything from it why am i not  feeling that i'm learning something new  this was just again  a movie that the visuals felt unique and  fresh but the story did not you know  i've seen these story beats before over  and over again i've seen this message  before over and over again i've seen  this twist over and over again so  that's where i was incredibly  disappointed with this film and it's not  saying that i didn't like the film  though because i really like the film i  think it's super entertaining and i  think  it has one of the best scores we've had  in years i think having the same  cinematography always does doesn't hurt  him at all he's amazing and the  cinematography here was amazing i think  the production design the costume design  is awesome and  i do wish there was more william the foe  right because he's just a scene stealer  in all this and i also was a little  disappointed with anya taylor joyce  character i don't think she really has  much to do i don't think it's a great  character but she's great alexander  skarsgard crushes it right i think he  was perfect for this role i thought  nicole kidman i don't know if she didn't  fit the part that great but nothing  really going on there that impressed me  i thought the standout was actually  clay's bang here as the uncle i thought  he was great i wasn't familiar with him  before this but  i know he played dracula recently but  i'm excited to see what he does because  he just was the best part of this film  to me but that's the thing is like at  the end of the day you watching you're  okay you know what that was a really  good episode of game of thrones that's  what i felt like i watched and that's  disappointing because with robert eggers  you want to leave thinking about it  talking about it you know letting it  just  soak in on you i don't think that  happens here i think it's really just  this box office blockbuster now he's  doing and that is just something i'm  just a little worried about and i don't  want it to go that trajectory for him  where he starts escaping what he's you  know known for which makes him in that  different level of directors and writers  but that's something confusing me too  because it's so hard to review something  like this because for what it is it does  an excellent job like there's i don't  fault it for anything in that department  of visuals or directing but it's again  that story it's just okay i've seen all  these story beats before i've seen this  twist i've seen this message so that's  what is just so so disappointing and  that's why i confused with some critics  who will be like oh this was his  masterpiece and his best yet but it's  like so did you not value where he  really shines in his writing the last  two films he did that you're thinking  this is his masterpiece what was it  about this just because it had a bigger  budget because i had bigger action that  it's a better film that doesn't make  sense to me i think that actually takes  it down so i'm giving this one an 8.1  please don't confuse that i'm thinking i  didn't like this film i really like this  film and i think that it's something i  would definitely see again in theaters  just to have fun but it's just strange  to me robert eggers is doing a film that  i can shut my brain down on and not  really have to really think let me know  though maybe you guys had a different  reaction to it this is how i feel though  and i think it's definitely number three  out of his films i still think the witch  was the best then the lighthouse and  this was you know a full point drop in  quality which is really disappointing  but still solid and again  in those other departments that's not  writing awesome but  writing is the most important and i need  to feel something and i need to think  about something when i go to the movies  and if you're just going to make another  revenant  mixed with game of thrones and a little  bit of lion king sprinkled in you know  okay cool like i'm happy i can see you  can work well with a big budget but  i just feel like he is better than this  he's more of a higher ceiling and i hope  he doesn't start falling into things  that are gonna kind of keep him boxed in  because that's what i was worried about  when i saw what he was planning to do  next and that's exactly what ended up  happening so it's strange to me they  don't see that happening ahead of time  either so  who knows but let me know what you  thought i'd love to hear your thoughts i  read every comment and try to respond as  many as i can let me know what you  thought about all of robert eggers films  and where would you kind of rank them  i'd like to hear that as well and please  follow me at steve varley show on  twitter instagram and tick tock for more  of me and i'll see you next time

